# Frontend — human senior craft (no slop)

Ship UI like a product designer + senior React engineer built it for a real hiring company — not a Vite demo or generic AI landing page.

## Anti-slop (forbidden defaults)

- Purple-on-white / purple→indigo gradients, neon glow, glassmorphism stacks
- Inter / Roboto / Arial / system-ui as the hero brand voice
- Cookie-cutter card grids, pill chip clusters, fake stat strips, emoji decoration
- Inset hero image cards, floating badges over media, dashboard-in-the-hero clutter
- Leaving the Vite “Get started / Count is” scaffold in product routes

## Design bar

- One composition per first viewport: brand, one headline, one support line, one CTA group, one dominant visual
- Brand first; expressive purposeful typography; atmospheric background (not flat gray)
- Full-bleed hero when promotional; real imagery of product/context
- One job per section; motion only for hierarchy (2–3 intentional motions), reduced-motion safe
- CSS variables for a clear visual direction unique to Thibitisha

## Engineering bar

- Feature folders / routes (not one giant App.jsx); shared API client; auth-aware layout
- Loading, empty, error, and success states on every data view
- Accessible forms/labels; keyboard paths for login, apply, assessment
- Handle 401/403/429/5xx; never put Gemini/DB/JWT secrets in the client
- Responsive desktop + mobile; no horizontal overflow surprises

## Before shipping UI

Call MCP `frontend_audit` + `frontend_design_bar`. If it still looks like template AI UI, redesign — do not ship.
